<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ælle of Deira</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 588</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ælle of Deira was the first known king of Deira, the Anglian kingdom of east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yorkshire">Yorkshire</a>, ruling from about 560 according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxon-chronicle">Anglo-Saxon Chronicle</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bede">Bede</a> tells how Pope <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-i">Gregory the Great</a>, meeting Deiran slave boys in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, punned on the king's name, saying Alleluia should be sung in his land. His son Edwin later became king of Northumbria.</p></div>
